{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/767099-slight-compensation-for-dual-wielding-balance-question","id":767099,"title":"Slight compensation for dual wielding? (Balance Question)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-16T08:41:35-08:00","id":767099,"title":"Slight compensation for dual wielding? (Balance Question)","content":"New DM just looking to tweak the game a little to my group's liking.<br /> <br /> My group and I come from a background where different fighting styles have some mechanical differences to them. I have no issue with the abstraction of combat styles within Scion as it is currently but I was considering creating a slight benefit to dual wielding. Currently it would seem there isn't any functional difference between using a single 1h weapon or two 1h weapons. In my mind the player would be essentially giving up access to having a free hand purely based on the flavor of dual wielding. My idea was to give dual wielding a niche within the DV system. Every attack from a dual wielding character would reduce the targets defense by 2 rather than the normal one till their next turn. A multiple attack action would then reduce their defense for a total of 4 (or maybe 3 if 4 was a bit too much).<br /> <br /> So a few questions from those more experienced with the system.<br /> <br /> 1. How important is having an open hand in Scion? Seems not a whole lot considering how abstract things can be.<br /> 2. How do you personally handle dual wielding in your games? Do you modify damage or speed slightly and just consider them one weapon in functionality? I assume you would then avoid giving them player any future relics that would force him to need a free hand.<br /> 3. Do you feel the above change would impact things negatively? I read that DVs can shoot through the roof to the point that it seems almost impossible to damage people sometimes. I figured this change would give a counter to these high DVs if you coordinate rapid attacks before single big hits.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 11-16-2015, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T13:00:37-08:00","id":767238,"title":"","content":"1) Not important at all<br /> 2) I have it function no differently from using a two-handed weapon, a one-handed weapon or no weapon at all. I treat all attacks as essentially the same. <br /> 3) Yes, it would. Because if you give dual-wielding an advantage, what is the <i>dis</i>advantage? Why wouldn't <i>everyone</i> do it, since it's dramatically better? Now instead of making dual wielding plausible, you've made <i>not</i> doing it implausible. <br /> <br /> You're absolutely right, though, combat in Scion goes bonkers after Legend 4, but the whole game really does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T13:50:18-08:00","id":767302,"title":"","content":"I'd say the disadvantage to it being it's equally damaging to a 1h weapon. A 2h would always do more damage than dual wielding but dual wielding would allow you to swing those high DVs in a more reasonable direction and function as a support damage type character. I read a comment that all melee combat essentially feels the same. A disadvantage im seeing based on this suggestion is the benefit of a single 1h weapon has been eradicated. Of course the options after this realization would be to drop the change entirely or give a benefit to single wielding such as better defense due to them having a free hand to grab limbs and isolate targets that attack them. Creating the dynamic of 2h = damage, dual wield = anti high DV/setting up bigger hits, single 1h = better damage mitigation. Didn't see any shields listed to fill the tankier niche.<br /> <br /> Also, how does everyone handle grappling while holding weapons? Does everyone just assume weapons get sheathed/cant be used as part of a grapple and it just goes into some epic god wrestling scene?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, when you say you have it function the exact same do you mean you simply take the stats of a single weapon and just label it as dual wielding? Essentially ignoring the offhand weapon entirely for flavor? It seemed to me that the Donnie Iconic's pistols were 1 damage higher than a single gun. In this case it seems they gave him +1 damage innately for the 2nd Beretta. In that case, maybe I should just do that instead. Less interesting but certainly less risky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 11-16-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T15:39:10-08:00","id":768148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/767099-slight-compensation-for-dual-wielding-balance-question?p=767302#post767302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say the disadvantage to it being it's equally damaging to a 1h weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a disadvantage. That's equality with a 1h weapon. That makes 1h weapons <b>always</b> inferior to dual-wielding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/767099-slight-compensation-for-dual-wielding-balance-question?p=767302#post767302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A 2h would always do more damage than dual wielding but dual wielding would allow you to swing those high DVs in a more reasonable direction and function as a support damage type character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of how terribly Scion combat works, that's not really much of a benefit. Especially since weapon stats are so variable. Load up on the +damage bonuses for your dual-wielding weapons and now you're swinging all the damage of a war mace (or <b>much </b>more!!)..twice. With DV reduction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/767099-slight-compensation-for-dual-wielding-balance-question?p=767302#post767302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read a comment that all melee combat essentially feels the same. A disadvantage im seeing based on this suggestion is the benefit of a single 1h weapon has been eradicated. Of course the options after this realization would be to drop the change entirely or give a benefit to single wielding such as better defense due to them having a free hand to grab limbs and isolate targets that attack them. Creating the dynamic of 2h = damage, dual wield = anti high DV/setting up bigger hits, single 1h = better damage mitigation. Didn't see any shields listed to fill the tankier niche.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you give 1-handed weapons a benefit, sure, then things would be more balanced. But if they're the 'baseline' and you buff dual-wielding.. then everyone should dual wield, forever. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/767099-slight-compensation-for-dual-wielding-balance-question?p=767302#post767302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, how does everyone handle grappling while holding weapons? Does everyone just assume weapons get sheathed/cant be used as part of a grapple and it just goes into some epic god wrestling scene?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, exactly that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/767099-slight-compensation-for-dual-wielding-balance-question?p=767302#post767302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Also, when you say you have it function the exact same do you mean you simply take the stats of a single weapon and just label it as dual wielding? Essentially ignoring the offhand weapon entirely for flavor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that. There is no mechanical effect at all to dual-wielding. You just have whatever weapon you have and if it's really two weapons, then that's fine. It's treated as a &quot;set&quot; instead of two distinct items. Even for Relics, I just stat the things as one Relic that has two parts. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/767099-slight-compensation-for-dual-wielding-balance-question?p=767302#post767302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seemed to me that the Donnie Iconic's pistols were 1 damage higher than a single gun. In this case it seems they gave him +1 damage innately for the 2nd Beretta. In that case, maybe I should just do that instead. Less interesting but certainly less risky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think their damage bonus is from being Relics. The second gun appears in Demigod and has a different <i>power</i>, but not different <i>stats</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T16:47:49-08:00","id":768173,"title":"","content":"Pretty much on the same page as you at this point but I still think they did boost Donnie's gun set based somewhat on it being two guns. In the Hero book they specifically explain his weapons and how they made them but exclude the dmg boost and how it got there. They say they are dual Berrettas with -1 speed, +1 accuracy, and two 1 dot unique powers. They list them as 4 points so this is in line with the costs as well. One gun makes you love someone and the other gun makes you hate someone. Same 'weapon' in functionality so the dmg increase is never factored. But hes an Iconic... so maybe they just tossed the extra dmg on for free just because hes Donnie Rhodes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T00:39:24-08:00","id":768329,"title":"","content":"Could also simply be that the writer didn't get the values right to start with, or that the weapons table changed later in editing. Scion is <b>full</b> of typos and editing mistakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T01:50:26-08:00","id":768355,"title":"","content":"Using the pre-generated characters as any kind of comparison is rarely wise. Respects to the writers and all, but there are some glaring mistakes both in typing, addition, and also of thinking. Victor Fingers' armour for one, and setting up Eric Donner, the team brick, with a pistol that will never hit for another.<br /> <br /> And while melee combat <i>does</i> look the same, remember that that's only <i>mechanically. </i>In the <i>narrative</i> of the game a dual wielder has awesome stunting options that could and should be used, and that a good ST should run with, that provide all manner of advantages. Just not in the bare bones mechanics.<br /> <br /> It's not ideal, and when you compare it to many other game systems where dual wielding provides you with an extra attack or some other mechanical bonus it seems weak, but when you look to the narrative you do have some advantages.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you might consider a dual wielder's second attack with a weapon a -2 dice penalty rather than a -4 dice penalty. It makes dual wielding a little better but, honestly, with how broken combat gets that doesn't really mean much once you factor Epics and certain Boons into things. Some people will jump on that two dice discount and decide that every character they make has to be a dual wielder and some won't. In the end, after Hero level, it doesn't make a large difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}